$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):AMD
$DATUM polyvinyl pyridine complex
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Reaction Procedure To a 100-ml,
round-bottom flask, aldehyde (3 mmol), methanol (10 ml), and Ru-PVP (0.05
g) were added. The solution was refluxed (68-70°C) until the aldehyde was
consumed (thin-layer chromatography). The reaction mixture was allowed to
cool to room temperature and filtered, and the catalysts were washed with
methanol (3 × 10 ml). The filtrate was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The product was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (60-120 mesh) with eluent [EtOAc-pet. ether
(60-80) =6:94]. For the compounds 2b, 2c, and 2d, no purification was
needed as they were obtained in pure form. 2b, yield 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemoselective protection of aldehydes in the presence of ketones using
RuPVP complex as a heterogeneous catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
