$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure of the protection of aldehyde with alcohol in the
presence of ATPB. To a solution of 3-phenylpropanal (1) (287 mg, 2.14
mmol) in 2 mL of methanol was added ATPB (85 mg, 0.21 mmol) and the
solution was stirred at RT. The reaction was complete in 20 min. The
solution was concentrated and the residue was chromatographed on silica
gel to give the desired product 1a (358.8 mg, 1.99 mmol) in 93% yield.
3-Phenylpropionaldehyde dimethyl acetal (1a), yield 93%. 1H NMR (CDCl3,
400 MHz) δ 1.90-1.95 (m, 2H, PhCH2CH2-), 2.67 (dd, J = 8.2 and 6.1 Hz,
2H, PhCH2-), 3.33 (s, 6H, -OCH3), 4.37 (t, J = 5.7 Hz, 1H, -CH(OCH3)2),
7.18-7.28 (m, 5H, Ar-H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 30.8 (PhCH2CH2-),
34.1 (PhCH2-), 52.7 (-OCH3), 103.8 (-CH(OCH3)2), 125.8, 128.4, 141.6
(4°). IR (KBr) 2958, 1604, 1493, 1457, 1383 cm-1. MS m/z (relative
intensity): 180 (M+, 4), 148 (89), 91 (100), 75 (96). HRMS calcd. for
C11H16O2: 180.1151. Found: 180.1147.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative method using solid-supported catalyst,
acetonyltriphenylphosphonium bromide supported on polystyrene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Acetonyltriphenylphosphonium Bromide and Its Polymer-Supported Analogues
as Catalysts for the Protection of Carbonyl Compounds as Acetals or
Thioacetals
