$DATUM 14808-79-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Acetalization of
Carbonyl Compounds A mixture of aldehyde or ketone 1 (5 mmol), (EtO)3CH 2
(15 mmol), and TiO2/SO42- (100 mg) was stirred at reflux for the length
of time indicated in Table 1. Absolute alcohol (5 mL) was added. The
progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC or GC. After completion of
the reaction, the catalyst was filtered off and washed with Et2O. The
filtrate was washed with 40% NaHSO3 (15 mL) and brine (2 x 15 mL)
successively and dried (MgSO4). Evaporation of the solvent under reduced
pressure gave almost pure product(s). Further purification was proceeded
by column chromatograhy on silica gel (light petroleum-ether as eluent)
to afford pure diethyl acetal 3. Table 1, Entry 2, yield 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A highly efficient and chemoselective method for acetalization of
carbonyl compounds catalyzed by TiO2/SO42- solid superacid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ma, Yan-Ran; Jin, Tong-Shou; Shi, Sheng-Xun; Li, Tong-Shuang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2003), 33(12), 2103-2108

