$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 9,10,23,24,37,38-Hexaoxatrispiro[7.2.1111.2.1125.28]- octatriacontane
(6f). 1,1-Dimethoxycyclooctane 1f (0.447 g, 2.6 mmol) was added to a
suspension of 1,1’-dihydroperoxydi- (cyclododecyl)peroxide 2d (0.862 g, 2
mmol) in THF (8 mL). A solution of BF3·Et2O (0.17 g, 1.2 mmol) in THF
(0.5 mL) was added to the reaction mixture at 20 °C. Then the mixture was
stirred at 20-25 °C for 5 h. A major portion of solvent (~3/4) was
evaporated from the reaction mixture, and cooled MeOH (15 mL) was added.
The white crystals that precipitated were filtered off and washed with
cooled MeOH (3 x 5 mL). The purity of the compounds was ~95%.
Analytically pure 6f (1.01 g, 18.8 mmol) was isolated by column
chromatography on SiO2 (petroleum etherethyl acetate, 20:1). Yield 94%.
9,10,23,24,37,38-Hexaoxatrispiro[7.2.1111.2.1125.28]- octatriacontane
(6f), 1.01 g, 18.8 mmol, yield 94% Mp = 198-200 °C (MeOH). (Mp8d )
185-187 °C). Rf 0.86 (TLC, PE-EA, 20:1). 1H NMR (250.13 MHz) δ: 1.20-1.84
(m, 58H). 13C NMR (62.9 MHz) δ: 19.4, 22.0, 22.2, 25.0, 26.0, 26.2, 26.7,
26.8, 28.1, 28.3, 111.5, 111.6. Anal. Calcd for C32H58O6: C, 71.33; H,
10.85. Found: C, 71.57; H, 10.46.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
