$DATUM General Procedure for Preparation of 3g and 3h.Salicyclic alcohol 2 (92
mg, 0.30 mmol), aldehyde (0.20 mmol), P2O5 (~0.2-0.3 mmol), and p-TsOH
(3.8mg, 0.020 mmol) in 1mL of benzene were stirred at room temperature
for 8 h. The reaction mixture was concentrated under vacuum and purified
by flash chromatography, eluted with Petroleum ether/ethylacetate = 20/1,
to afford the desired cyclic ketals.3g, 85mg (93%). Rf 0.43 (petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate = 20/1); 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.41-7.38(m, 2 H),
7.29-7.22(m, 8 H), 6.85(dd, J = 8.8, 0.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.76(dd, J = 8.9, 3.0
Hz, 1 H), 6.45(d, J =2.8 Hz), 3.65(s, 3 H), 1.76-1.71(m, 2 H),
1.52-1.34(m, 2 H), 1.32-1.11(m, 15 H), 0.88(t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3 H); 13C NMR
(100MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.2, 147.7, 146.5, 144.9, 128.8, 128.5, 128.22,
128.18, 127.8, 127.6,126.5, 118.9, 115.6, 114.2, 102.7, 81.4, 56.0, 41.4,
32.3, 31.4, 30.2, 30.0, 29.8, 25.2, 24.0. 23.1, 14.6; IR(neat) 3060,
2927, 2854, 1600, 1494, 1465, 1447, 1423, 1378, 1264, 1207; HRMS(ESI) m/e
calcd. for (M+ Na+) 481.2713, found 481.2720.
