$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Acetals 1-4 and 6; General Procedure10 The
aldehyde (1 equiv) and the corresponding trialkyl orthoformate (1 to 1.5
equiv) were mixed in a flask containing APTS (p-TsOH·H2O, 0.002 equiv).
The mixture was stirred overnight at r.t., then directly distilled under
reduced pressure to yield the acetal. 1,1-Dimethoxy-3-methylbutane (6)
From 3-methylbutyraldehyde (5 mL, 46 mmol), trimethyl orthoformate (7.5
mL, 69 mmol) and APTS (18 mg, 92 mmol); yield: 5.7 g (93%); colorless
oil. bp 62 °C/60 Torr. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.44 (t, 1 H, J = 6
Hz), 3.30 (s, 6 H), 1.70 (m, 1 H), 1.48 (dd, 2 H, J = 6, 6.8 Hz), 0.92
(d, 6 H, J = 6.4 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 103.1, 52.4, 41.1,
24.3, 22.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iron(III) chloride catalysis of the acetal-ene reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
