$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Acetals 1-4 and 6; General Procedure10 The aldehyde (1 equiv) and the
corresponding trialkyl orthoformate (1 to 1.5 equiv) were mixed in a
flask containing APTS (p-TsOH·H2O, 0.002 equiv). The mixture was stirred
overnight at r.t., then directly distilled under reduced pressure to
yield the acetal. 1-(3,3-Diethoxypropyl)benzene (3) From
2-phenylpropionaldehyde (5 mL, 37.7 mmol), triethyl orthoformate (9.39
mL, 56.5 mmol) and APTS (14 mg, 75 mmol); yield: 7.2 g (92%); colorless
oil. bp 106 °C/10 Torr. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.16-7.31 (m, 5 H),
4.50 (t, 1 H, J = 5.6 Hz), 3.66 (qd, 1 H, J = 7.2, 9.6 Hz), 3.51 (qd, 1
H, J = 7.2, 9.6 Hz), 2.70 (t, 2 H, J = 8 Hz), 1.96 (td, 2 H, J = 5.6, 8
Hz), 1.23 (dd, 3 H, J = 7.2, 7.2 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
141.7, 128.3, 128.2, 125.8, 102.1, 61.0, 35.0, 31.0, 15.3.
