$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4.0 Characterization data 2.0 Aldehyde acetalization catalyzed by 22
-general procedure A 20 mL reaction vial containing a stirring bar was
charged with 22 (0.05 mmol), fitted with a septum and flushed with argon.
The appropriate aldehyde (0.50 mmol) was added followed by dry methanol
(1.25 mL, 0.38 M) via syringe. The solution was then stirred at room
temperature for 24 h. When conversion was judged to be either complete or
>95% (by 1H-NMR spectroscopic analysis) the reaction was quenched with
PhNHNH2 and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude product was then
purified by flash-chromatography. 4.0 Characterization data Benzaldehyde
dimethyl acetal (3, Table 2, entry 1) The desired dimethyl acetal was
obtained following the general procedure using catalyst 22 (12.5 mg, 0.03
mmol), methanol (6.7 mL) and benzaldehyde (340 μL, 3.34 mmol). After
purification of the crude material by flash chromatography the product 3
was obtained as a pale yellow liquid (466 mg, 92%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 3.37
(s, 6H), 5.42 (s, 1H), 7.34-7.42 (m, 3H), 7.47-7.49 (m, 2H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 52.3, 102.7, 126.2, 127.8, 128.0, 137.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on catalysts and stoichiometry of catalyst, recyclable
catalyst, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unexpected catalysis: aprotic pyridinium ions as active and recyclable
Bronsted acid catalysts in protic media
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Procuranti, Barbara; Connon, Stephen J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(21), 4935-4938

