$DATUM Benzaldehyde dibenzyl acetal (Table 2, run 1) To a mixture of FeCl3 (2.0
mg, 0.012 mmol) and benzaldehyde (61 μl, 0.60 mmol) were added
benzyloxytrimethylsilane (284 μl, 1.44 mmol) at 0 °C under argon
atmosphere. The resultant mixture was stirred for 2 h and quenched with
saturated sodium hydrogencarbonate. The organic materials were extracted
with Et2O and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. The solvent was
evaporated and benzaldehyde dibenzyl acetal (172.5 mg, 92%) was isolated
by thin-layer chromatography on silica gel (ether : hexane = 1 : 10,
including Et3N). The product gave satisfactory 1H and 13C NMR, IR
spectra. Benzaldehyde dibenzyl acetal, yield 172.5 mg, 92% 1H NMR (CDCl3,
δ ) 7.57 (d, 2H, J = 6.8 Hz), 7.41-7.30 (m, 13H), 5.77 (s, 1H), 4.69 (s,
4H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, δ ) 138.20, 138.04, 128.54, 128.39, 127.82, 127.60,
126.89, 100.37, 67.03. IR (neat, cm-1) 3063, 3030, 2871, 1605, 1496,
1453, 1354, 1206, 1024, 735, 698, 601.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
