$DATUM 3,4,5-Tris-benzyloxy-2-benzyloxymethyl-6-(2-[1,3]dioxolan-2-yl-ethoxy)-tetrahydro-pyran
(33). The mixture of aldehyde 32 (100 mg, 0.168 mmol), p-TsOH.H2O (3 mg,
0.017 mmol), and DMF (0.5 mL) was placed into the 60 °C bath on rotary
evaporator for 5 h under vacuum. Workup as usual followed by flash
chromatography (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 3/1, Rf 0.4) afforded the
title compound 33, yield 98 mg, 92%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.25-7.36
(m, 18 H), 7.11-7.14 (m, 2 H), 4.97-5.01 (m, 2 H), 4.75-4.84 (m, 4 H),
4.60-4.66 (m, 2 H), 4.46 (d, J = 11.7 Hz, 2 H), 3.89-3.40 (m, 3 H),
3.72-3.87 (m, 5 H), 3.62-3.67 (m, 2 H), 3.53-3.59 (m, 2 H), 1.95-2.06 (m,
2 H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 138.8, 138.3, 138.2, 137. 9, 128.39,
128.35, 128.34, 128.31, 127.94, 127.90, 127.8, 127.7, 127.6, 127.5,
102.1, 97.0, 82.0, 80.00, 77.6, 75.7, 75.1, 73.4, 73.0, 70.1, 68.4, 64.8,
63.7, 33.9; IR(neat) 3088, 3063, 3030, 2883, 1497, 1454, 1361, 1142,
1072, 1028, 737, 697; HRMS (ESI) m/e calcd for C39H44O8Na, 663.2934,
found 663.2935.
