$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Preparation of 3g and
3h.Salicyclic alcohol 2 (92 mg, 0.30 mmol), aldehyde (0.20 mmol), P2O5
(~0.2-0.3 mmol), and p-TsOH (3.8mg, 0.020 mmol) in 1mL of benzene were
stirred at room temperature for 8 h. The reaction mixture was
concentrated under vacuum and purified by flash chromatography, eluted
with Petroleum ether/ethylacetate = 20/1, to afford the desired cyclic
ketals.3g, 85mg (93%). Compound 3h, 85mg (91%). Rf 0.2 (petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate = 20/1); 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.44-7.41(m, 2 H),
7.30-7.19(m, 8 H), 7.05-7.02(m, 2 H), 6.88(d, J = 8.9 Hz, 1 H),
6.81-6.75(m, 3 H), 6.46(d, J= 2.9 Hz, 1 H), 3.74(s, 3 H), 3.63(s, 3 H),
2.84-2.69(m, 2 H), 2.12-2.00(m, 2 H); 13C NMR (100MHz,CDCl3) δ 157.6,
152.9, 147.3, 145.8, 144.4, 134.0, 129.2, 128.3, 128.1, 127.8, 127.4,
127.3, 126.2, 118.5,115.1, 113.8, 113.7, 101.7, 81.1, 55.5, 55.2, 43.2,
28.9, 25.0; IR (neat) 3059, 2998, 2938, 2834, 1612,1584, 1512, 1494,
1447, 1423, 1378, 1300, 1245; HRMS(ESI) m/e calcd. for (M + Na+)
489.2034, found489.2056.
