$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Acetalization of 16a; Conversion of 16a to 16c. A mixture of dione 16a
(20 mg, 0.06 mmol), 2,2-dimethylpropane-1,3-diol (8 mg, 0.08 mmol), PTSA
(3 mg), and benzene (10 mL) was refluxed for 12 h with a Dean-Stark water
separator. Usual workup and removal of solvent furnished a residue, which
was purified by column chromatography using silica gel. Elution with 35%
ethyl acetate-hexane. Mono-acetal 16c (23 mg, 91%). This sample was found
to be identical (mp, IR, and 1H NMR) to the sample 16c derived from
mono-acetal 4c. 16c: mp 251 °C; IR (KBr) 1860, 1836, 1777,1738, 1227,
1086 cm-1; 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.55-6.40 (2H, m), 3.95 (1H, dd, J 1
= 8.8 Hz, J 2 = 3.7 Hz), 3.70 (1H, d, J = 11.6 Hz), 3.60-3.39 (6H, m),
3.32-3.26 (1H, m), 2.66-2.58 (2H, m), 2.50-2.39 (2H, m), 2.27-2.19 (1H,
m), 1.80 (1H, 1/2 ABq, J = 11.2 Hz), 1.51 (1H, 1/2 ABq, J = 10.8 Hz),
1.18 (3H, s), 0.77 (3H, s); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 211.7, 173.2,
172.9, 134.2, 132.5, 103.6, 73.6, 70.9, 54.1, 50.2, 48.5, 48.3, 44.3,
43.6, 41.9, 40.8, 40.5, 39.7, 38.7, 32.5, 32.4, 29.9, 23.7, 21.9. Anal.
Calcd for C24H24O6: C, 70.58; H, 5.92. Found: C, 70.65; H, 5.95.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Dean-Stark trap used, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Role of Heteroatoms in Diastereofacial Control in Cycloaddition to a
Dissymmetric Cyclohexa-1,3-diene Moiety in a Polycyclic Framework.
Remarkable Stereodirecting Influence of Distal Protective Groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mehta, Goverdhan; Uma, R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2000), 65(6), 1685-1696

